        "content": "$3(n - 7)$",
        "rationale": "This is 3 times the number that is 7 less than $n$."
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "content": "$3n + 7$",
        "rationale": "“Less than” means subtract, not add."
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "“3 times $n$” is $3n$. “7 less than” something means take 7 away from it, so the expression is $3n - 7$.",
    "hints": [
