    "explanation": "(a) $a - b = 4$, so $T = 2 \\times 16 - (3)(-1) = 32 + 3 = 35$. (b) $a - b = 1$, so $T = 2 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = 2\\frac{1}{4}$. (c) $a - b = -2 - (-5) = 3$, so $T = 18 - 10 = 8$.",
    "workedSolution": "**(a)** $a - b = 3 - (-1) = 4$; $2 \\times 4^2 = 32$; $ab = 3 \\times (-1) = -3$; $T = 32 - (-3) = 35$.\n\n**(b)** $a - b = \\frac{1}{2} - \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 1$; $2 \\times 1^2 = 2$; $ab = -\\frac{1}{4}$; $T = 2 + \\frac{1}{4} = 2.25$.\n\n**(c)** $a - b = -2 - (-5) = 3$; $2 \\times 3^2 = 18$; $ab = (-2)(-5) = 10$; $T = 18 - 10 = 8$.",
    "hints": [
